WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.169
Ho, ho, ho!

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:06.760
Merry Christmas, Happy Holidays, and Freaky
Festivus to you all from your good friends

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.000
at SCP Explained!

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.660
Deck the halls with boughs of SCP-407-induced
plant life, because today we’re gonna hit

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.650
you with the kind of Christmas Cheer you just
can’t contain!

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:24.110
Hang your stockings, pour a tall glass of
eggnog, and slip on your most hideous yuletide

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.900
sweater, because this is A Keter Kinda Christmas!

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.080
We’ve discussed Christmas anomalies both
in-depth and in passing on this channel before,

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:40.399
like SCP-4666, the positively terrifying Yule
Man, whose ritual Christmastime slayings strike

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:43.590
fear into the hearts of families everywhere.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:50.680
Or SCP-784, Christmas Cheer, a community where
it’s Christmas every day, and anyone who

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:56.590
refuses to show the proper spirit is dragged
off and given a forcible reeducation in the

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.490
reason for the season.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:05.080
There’s even the pitiful SCP-193x3, a fat,
sweaty, and perpetually drunk middle-aged

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.720
man in a Santa suit who has Irish cream for
blood.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.500
Reminds me of my Uncle Frank.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.980
But today, we’re dealing with something
REALLY special: A Christmas variety show hosted

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:20.520
by everyone’s favorite anomalous Foundation
researcher…

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.250
SCP-963!

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:27.689
Sorry, sorry, we mean Dr. Bright.

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:32.260
Dr. Bright is getting ready to receive guests
for his Christmas party like no other, and

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.399
the good news is, we’re all invited!

00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:39.200
There’s going to be stories, songs, comedy,
and more cameos than you could shake a Yule

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.200
log at!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.759
So get comfortable - It’s going to be a
fun one.

00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:46.200
But first, a quick message from this episode’s
sponsors:

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.360
The fine folks at the Shark Punching Center,
the first and last line of defense between

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.619
us and those dark-eyed subaquatic menaces!

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:57.729
And of course, the latest giggletastic product
from our good pals at the Dr. Wondertainment

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:01.540
Toy Company, a perfect stocking filler for
the Christmas season.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:06.159
That’s right - We’re talking about Spider
Party; just add water for eighty thousand

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.030
legs worth of arachnoFUNbia!

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.280
Warning: Parental supervision required.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.170
Your definition of arachnofunbia may differ
from that used by Dr. Wondertainment.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.280
Avoid use of this product if you are sensitive
to spider venom.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.220
Not for use in households with pets or which
are situated on reclaimed toxic waste dumps

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.340
and/or Indian burial grounds.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.870
Dr. Wondertainment is not responsible for
any cases of spideritis, spiderosis, or spidermania

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:23.880
caused by use of this product.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:27.310
Not to be used for gambling purposes without
the express written consent of Dr. Wondertainment.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.950
Oh, and of course, an additional thank you
to our friends at the Manna Charitable Foundation

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.840
for their generous grant!

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.330
More on that one later!

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:41.350
While Dr. Bright prepared for guests, SCP-1845
- a collection of freakishly intelligent animals

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:47.510
including a raccoon, a crow, a baby pig, a
chicken, and a fox by the name of King Eugenio

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.570
- prepared a dress rehearsal for a nativity
scene.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.730
Conflict erupted when the Chicken kept flubbing
her lines, and the other cast members found

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.280
it strange that King Eugenio insisted on playing
the Baby Jesus himself.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.340
By all accounts, he was kind of a nightmare
to work with thanks to his massive ego.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:10.460
The situation worsened when SCP-329-J - a
floating YIELD sign that believes it’s a

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.540
ghost - turned up, claiming to be the Ghost
of Christmas Past, and started bothering King

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.610
Eugenio.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:19.390
If you think this is weird, you’re going
to have real trouble with the rest of this,

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.060
so we recommend sitting back, putting your
feet up, and just rolling with it, cause it’s

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.320
only going to get stranger from here.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.150
Anyway, back to the living room of Dr. Jack
Bright, who was singing a special SCP Foundation

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.260
parody of the Christmas carol “God Rest
Ye, Merry Gentlemen”, when the first set

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:36.810
of guests arrived.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.970
It was Dr. Charles Odgen Gears, a famously
humorless Foundation Senior Researcher, dressed

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.130
in his own adorably gaudy Christmas attire.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:49.890
But he wasn’t alone - He’d brought special
musical guests, Captain and Tennille,

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:55.300
the classic 1970s duo responsible for hits
such as “Love Will Keep Us Together” and

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.300
“Muskrat Love.”

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:00.200
They’d actually attended gigs like this
before, but thanks to the beauty of Class-A

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.770
Amnestics, it was all new to them.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:07.020
Let’s ignore the murky ethical implications
of that and keep on trucking.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:12.420
Next, this Christmas extravaganza careened
into another anomalous skit, this one featuring

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:18.890
SCP-1192 - A little boy named Timmy who was
somehow transformed into a bird - and Count

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:27.260
Rockula, a badass heavy metal aficionado summoned
by SCP-1987-J’s anomalously sick chord progression.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.750
Timmy was naturally a little upset about being
trapped as a bird, and thus, he was unable

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.760
to spend Christmas with his family.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.500
Count Rockula, being the Lord of Ultimate
Rockness, refused to let the poor bird/boy

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.500
suffer.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.070
In order to cheer him up, he grabbed his guitar
and launched into a spirited rock and roll

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:48.600
Christmas carol, with much racier lyrics than
you’d probably expect from a wholesome Christmas

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.600
tune.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.660
The Count was left feeling a little nervous
afterwards when Timmy started asking him what

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.370
a “camel toe” was.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:01.300
The sooner we get away from this little disaster
of a segment, the better…

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.780
Back to Dr. Bright’s living room once more.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.230
The good anomalous doctor has just finished
telling a hilarious anecdote to Dr. Gears

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:13.390
and 1970s music powerhouse Captain and Tenille,
when Dr. Gears took the opportunity to break

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:19.390
some bad news: A certain, very rowdy former
party guest had found out about this year’s

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:25.190
meet up, and he would likely be joining any
minute now, much to Bright’s dismay.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:34.270
As if on cue, the door burst open, and there
stood SCP-076-2, also known as Able, the immortal

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:39.310
swordsman, wearing an ugly Christmas sweater
and a Santa hat, yelling “Did somebody say

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.690
par-taaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaay?”

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:44.260
Dr. Bright was mortified.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.500
At last year’s party,
Able had gotten tanked on hard eggnog and

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:52.080
embarrassed them all in front of Country Music
Legend Willie Nelson with his antics.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.060
Specifically, he’d stolen a local sleigh
and used it to run over Bright’s grandmother.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:02.290
However, Able insisted that this time around,
he’d be well-behaved.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:05.190
Only time would tell if that prediction held
any water.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:10.280
He began to sing a personalized parody of
“Away In A Manger” in a grating falsetto

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.590
voice as an act of penance.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:17.570
Let’s get away from those goofballs again
and hop over to another ace comedic duo: Lord

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:20.470
Blackwood and Wellington G. Wonderhorse.

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:27.390
Blackwood, also known as SCP-1867, is a telepathic
sea slug who believes he was once a galavanting

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.530
British noble and explorer.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:35.730
And Wellington, also known as SCP-1156, is
a talking horse with a thick cockney accent

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.370
and a dapper woolen scarf and top hat.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:43.000
This pair of talking creatures wished the
audience a very Merry Christmas, before engaging

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.000
in conversation.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.920
However, this didn’t get very far, as Lord
Blackwood couldn’t understand Wellington’s

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.580
thick cockney accent.

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:55.660
When Lord Blackwood got too frustrated to
go on, he called Wellington a horse’s ass.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.660
Everybody laughs.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.760
Roll on snare drums.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.420
Curtains.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.690
Back to Dr. Bright’s increasingly chaotic
Christmas house party.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:07.560
Able was already getting a little sloshed
and telling wild jokes, when another guest

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.590
appeared at the door.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:14.010
When Dr. Bright answered, he saw Dr. Rights,
a female fellow researcher, standing there

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.139
in a full-body trench coat.

00:07:16.139 --> 00:07:21.490
She expressed a desire to meet Dr. Bright
under the mistletoe, to which he replied,

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:24.590
“Rights, I didn't put up any mistletoe this
year.”

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:28.520
But Rights, obviously in the Christmas spirit,
with a smile on her face and with no concern

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:32.430
for the lack of mistletoe at the party, disrobed
from her trench coat.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:37.560
Donned in her hand-knitted, wool Christmas
two-piece, she began to dance toward Dr. Bright

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:43.330
while singing a parody of the saucy Christmas
hit, “Santa Baby” -

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:47.500
Uhhhh….Let’s cut to another word from
one of our sponsors:

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:51.911
The wonderful folks at the Manna Charitable
Foundation, the world’s leading anomalous

00:07:51.911 --> 00:07:52.911
charity group.

00:07:52.911 --> 00:07:56.880
In this sponsorship break, Manna Charitable
Foundation representative Sally Struthers

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:00.190
placed a small mechanical contraption on a
table and said:

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:02.639
“This is the Christmas Miracle Maker.

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:07.639
Thanks to state-of-the-art terraforming technology,
this durable and easy-to-use device, once

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:12.570
activated, will induce rapid and aggressive
climate change in order to transform its surrounding

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:17.780
environment into a perfect snowy winter's
day just in time for a white Christmas.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:22.590
The seed banks and genetic samples contained
within it will ensure that majestic evergreens

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:27.830
just right for decorating and reindeer perfect
for pulling a one-horse open sleigh will replace

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:32.519
all the local flora and fauna, and it can
even whip up a Christmas dinner with all the

00:08:32.519 --> 00:08:34.860
trimmings for those souls in need!

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:40.130
Every one of your donations puts us one step
closer to our goal of manufacturing and airdropping

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:44.360
15,000 of these units across Africa in time
for Christmas Eve.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:48.840
So please call in your pledge or write a check
today - and let them know it's Christmas time

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:49.840
again.”

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:50.840
Thank you, Sally.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:55.160
Let’s get back to Dr. Bright’s party now
things are looking a little more Safe For

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:58.140
Work - If only slightly, at least.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.770
Decorated Russian Mobile Task Force Operative
Agent Strelnikov had joined the party, and

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:07.310
was naturally beginning to make multiple jokes
about how much he hates Chechens, much to

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.150
the discomfort of everyone else in attendance.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:15.310
The other party guests tried to make him discuss
literally anything else, but he refused, repeatedly

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:18.290
circling back to telling stories about Chechens.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:22.640
He only broke from his diatribe to give a
rendition of the formerly popular Trololo

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:27.660
meme song, which he insisted was a traditional
Russian song of homecoming.

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:31.900
Back to King Eugenio the fox, who’d been
going through a parallel Christmas Carol narrative

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.560
this whole time during Dr. Bright’s story.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.190
The talking Yield sign was his Spirit of Christmas
Past, and while we sadly missed his Spirit

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:44.770
of Christmas Present, as we join him before
his own gravestone, we can see that his Spirit

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:50.270
of Christmas Yet To Come was SCP-173 - The
Sculpture.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:54.940
As The Sculpture pointed towards King Eugenio’s
grave in judgemental silence, Eugenio came

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.250
to terms with what a jerk he’d been.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:01.740
When he was freed from this horrible fantasy,
he realized that he needed to change his ways,

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.750
and thankfully, there was still time.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.750
Back to Dr. Bright’s Christmas Party, which
was in full swing.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:11.650
However, Captain and Tennille, who had been
in charge of cooking the Christmas goose,

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.380
had made a terrible mistake.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:18.740
They were told to run it through SCP-914 on
the Fine setting, which would create a wonderful

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:24.100
goose roast, but they instead ran it through
the Very Fine mode, turning it into a collection

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.220
of live goslings.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:28.990
However, in the greatest hour of need, a hero
rose.

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:34.600
Dr. Clef appeared at the door, dressed as
Santa Claus, with enough delicious clam chowder

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.010
for everyone!

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:43.000
And as the party guests enjoyed their chowder,
even more guests arrived: King Eugenio, Wellington,

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:49.021
SCP-173, Lord Blackwood, the Ghostly Yield
Sign, Count Rockula, Timmy the Bird, and even

00:10:49.021 --> 00:10:54.980
Sally Struthers, while the rest of the anomalous
animals formed a perfect nativity scene.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:59.580
While Count Rockula performed a Rock and Roll
rendition of “Come All Ye Faithful”, Dr.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:04.170
Bright was content that everyone here had
learned the true meaning of Christmas after

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:05.170
all.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:09.560
Even King Eugenio had learned a lot about
being more kind and compassionate to his fellow

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:10.560
beasts.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:16.520
With the help of Lord Blackwood, he obtained
SCP-662, The Butler’s Hand Bell, and used

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:21.399
it to summon Mr. Deeds, along with a delicious,
fully-cooked Christmas goose with all the

00:11:21.399 --> 00:11:22.399
trimmings.

00:11:22.399 --> 00:11:26.520
While Dr. Rights flirted with Able and the
other party guests prepared to enjoy their

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:32.580
chowder and goose, Dr. Bright wished everyone
a happy Christmas, with Timmy adding, “And

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.700
343 bless us, every one!”

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:39.960
We hope this little exploration into how the
Foundation celebrates Christmas has helped

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:44.760
your heart grow three sizes this day - and
not in the way it would if you ate a meal

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.270
off of SCP-807.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:52.100
Stay tuned for A Keter Kinda Hanukkah and
A Keter Kinda Kwanza - Coming soon!

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:59.250
Now go check out “SCP-4666 - The Yule Man”
and “Alaska Doomsday Weapon SCP-804 - World

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:03.649
Without Man” for more snow-swept havoc from
the SCP Foundation!

